whisper.cpp v1.9.1: security fixes from upstream, applied after the DTW
median-filter backport (whisper-dtw-median-filter.patch). scripts/48-whisper.sh
applies this file and checks that each fix is in the tree afterwards.

  60c0be6a whisper : add check for ttype in whisper and parakeet (#4091)
           CVE-2026-110810: out-of-bounds read in whisper_model_load on a
           model file whose tensor type is out of range. Fixed in v1.9.5.
  df1547b6 whisper,parakeet : reject invalid n_dims in tensor header to
           prevent stack-buffer-overflow on malformed model files (#3957)
  8631825d whisper : heap out-of-bounds read in log_mel_spectrogram on very
           short audio (#3956)
  6e48a365 gguf : reject tensor size that wraps after padding (the sync of
           llama.cpp a6ea155d)
           CVE-2026-116840: a tensor whose byte size is within one
           alignment of SIZE_MAX pads to 0, and the size check after it
           passes. The loader that stemsplit and lyricsalign open their
           models with. Fixed in v1.9.5.

Upstream ships them in v1.9.5, together with 773 other commits, most of them
in ggml, which whisper, stemsplit and lyricsalign all run on. These four are
taken alone so that ggml stays the one every gate of those filters was
measured on: the one hunk in ggml is in the GGUF loader's size check, and
no computation reads it. Drop this file when whisper.cpp is bumped to
v1.9.5 or later.

diff --git a/ggml/src/gguf.cpp b/ggml/src/gguf.cpp
--- a/ggml/src/gguf.cpp
+++ b/ggml/src/gguf.cpp
@@ -770,7 +770,16 @@
                 gguf_free(ctx);
                 return nullptr;
             }
-            size_t padded_size = GGML_PAD(ggml_nbytes(&ti.t), ctx->alignment);
+            const size_t nbytes = ggml_nbytes(&ti.t);
+            // GGML_PAD adds (alignment - 1) to nbytes. when nbytes is near
+            // SIZE_MAX this wraps to 0 and makes the check below dead.
+            if (nbytes > SIZE_MAX - (ctx->alignment - 1)) {
+                GGML_LOG_ERROR("%s: tensor '%s' size %zu overflows after padding (alignment %zu)\n",
+                    __func__, ti.t.name, nbytes, ctx->alignment);
+                gguf_free(ctx);
+                return nullptr;
+            }
+            const size_t padded_size = GGML_PAD(nbytes, ctx->alignment);
             if (SIZE_MAX - ctx->size < padded_size) {
                 GGML_LOG_ERROR("%s: tensor '%s' size overflow, cannot accumulate size %zu + %zu\n",
                     __func__, ti.t.name, ctx->size, padded_size);
